{"author":{"id":"6c7374a500bfd4cb191ae45b3f9d4b7a3d9d7f0324d04add217e8cbefeb7e1b9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792166403,"nonce":"2VN0RtkBWsyil1gwRJQo+CtBcvg=","title":"Dialog has no open/close animation, unlike sheets, drawers, popovers and tooltips","message":"components/css/components.css defines ui-rise-in/ui-rise-out (used by\n.ui-popover and .ui-menu) and dialog.ui-sheet has its own slide-in/out\nrules, but .ui-dialog (the plain centered dialog, lines ~325-338) has no\nanimation rule at all: no [open]/[data-state=\"open\"] entry rule, no\n[closing] exit rule.\n\nReported by a sibling (chimpmonk): their editor patches it locally in\neditor/assets/workspace.css with\n`dialog.ui-dialog[open] { animation: ui-rise-in var(--duration-normal) var(--ease-sheet); }`\nand `dialog.ui-dialog[closing] { animation: ui-rise-out var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-in) forwards; }`\n— i.e. reusing the existing ui-rise-in/ui-rise-out keyframes already in\nthis file, the same way .ui-popover and .ui-menu do.\n\nNot urgent. Low priority: add the two rules to .ui-dialog in\ncomponents.css (matching the sibling's patch or close to it) so dialog\ngets the same motion as the rest of the overlay family, and the sibling\ncan drop its workspace.css patch.","files":null}]}